    ; `layoutGrid` gathers the in-flow items and leaves an `isAbsolute` child
    ; out of the placement, which is right — an absolute box takes no track.
    ; What was missing is this: nothing laid it out afterwards either, so it
    ; kept zero size at the page origin. `contentHeight` is the rows' own
    ; height, used when the container has no definite one, so a percentage
    ; offset resolves against the box the grid actually came out as.
    fn layoutGridOutOfFlow:void (parent:EVGElement innerWidth:double contentHeight:double startX:double startY:double) {
        def n:int (parent.getChildCount())
        def i:int 0
        while (i < n) {
